30,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,I found that we lose an hour daily to copying records and have many misrouted deliveries because of inconsistent addresses.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,May,,"We have no available in-house developers until Q3, and the coordination group is severely understaffed. We can't just add more manual work.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's as I feared. Network coverage at plants is terrible and getting device approval is a nightmare. Any ""mobile"" solution is a fantasy.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The capital budget is frozen. We only have room in the recurring software allowance. Also, per-head licensing will make costs spiral as we scale.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I found that big projects requiring everyone to enter data always fail. Only small, specialized tools for one specific trade actually survive.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Ryuji, if the budget is frozen, does that mean we can only pick something that fits the software allowance?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,May,,"@Kenji, that's a great point. If we pick something that requires daily entry from everyone, it'll just fail and burn out the staff.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"Exactly. And if it requires site access or connectivity, it's dead on arrival. We need something internal and low-maintenance.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Yes, Daisuke. We must avoid high upfront capital costs and avoid per-user licensing if we want to keep it affordable long-term.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"So we need something narrow, internal, and not too demanding on everyone's time.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,The address errors and copying time are real problems. Maybe a tool to centralize that data would help?,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,May,,As long as it doesn't require a huge team to maintain or a bunch of developers we don't have.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"A central hub for data sounds more realistic than a field app, given the network issues I found.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"A fixed-fee project would be safer than a license-based one, given our budget constraints.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"Let's keep in mind that ""standardization"" often fails unless it's for a specific trade.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
