55,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Candidate C addresses the misrouted deliveries and the time lost to copying records. It solves the actual floor problems.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,May,,"Candidate D sounds like it adds more ""coordination"" work. Candidate C is a repository, which is more passive and less taxing on staff.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Candidate A is impossible due to the network and approval issues. Candidate C is internal, so it avoids the site-access nightmare.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Candidate C might involve per-user licenses if it's a hub, but if it's a fixed-fee build, it fits. B and D seem too vague on cost.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Candidate C is a ""standardization"" effort. I'm worried it'll be dropped if it requires everyone to update it daily.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, but the problem is that we have different addresses for the same firm. Fixing that is a specific, narrow goal.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, if we can get C as a fixed-fee project, it doesn't burden the developers as much as a complex app like A or D.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,Candidate B is just a studio; it doesn't solve the operational inefficiencies Daisuke mentioned. C is the only rational choice.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. A is out due to budget/network. D is too risky for staffing. C is the most stable if we manage the license.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"If it's just a searchable catalog for supplier records, it's more like a ""tool for a trade"" than a company-wide mandate. I can support that.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I feel much better knowing we are addressing the actual errors in the logs. I vote for C.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,May,,It's the least likely to break the rota if it's a central hub rather than a daily task for everyone. I'm for C.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,It's the only one that doesn't rely on conditions we can't control. C it is.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,It fits the software allowance better than a capital-heavy project. I vote C.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"Since we all agree it can be kept narrow and useful, I'll vote C too.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
